    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are square matrices of order <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> such that <math><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mfenced></math>, then <math><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></math> is equal to (where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;represent the transpose matrix and adjoint matrix of matrix&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math>&nbsp;represents the identity matrix of order&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>)",
